## 2. Free permitted uses

Subject to Sections 4–8, you may use, copy, modify, and redistribute the Software solely for the following **Permitted Noncommercial Uses**:

(a) Personal or family learning, private study, experimentation, and research not conducted for a paid client, employer's commercial offering, or revenue-generating product.

(b) Classroom teaching by teachers in public schools, nonprofit schools, and other genuinely noncommercial educational settings, provided the use is not part of a separately charged course, commercial training service, paid teaching-material product, or commercial institution's offering. Ordinary public school funding and standard school tuition or cost-recovery fees alone do not automatically turn otherwise noncommercial classroom teaching into a Commercial Use; the actual offering and purpose control.

(c) Free educational sharing and community collaboration without a commercial purpose, subject to the attribution and redistribution conditions below.

The permission in (b) does not extend to a commercial training institution merely because an individual teacher installs or runs the Software using a personal account or device.

## 3. Commercial Uses requiring advance written authorization

**You must obtain separate written commercial authorization from the Licensor BEFORE using the Software for any Commercial Use.** Commercial Use includes, whether conducted directly or indirectly:

(a) Using the Software in or for a commercial tutoring business, language training institution, commercial school, or other for-profit education or training provider, including internal preparation of teaching materials.

(b) Creating, preparing, supporting, delivering, or selling paid courses, paid tutoring, paid educational content, paid teaching materials, subscription content, or paid learning resources with the Software.

(c) Incorporating the Software or a modified version into any paid or commercial product, SaaS, API, application, workflow, service, customer deliverable, or product offered for commercial advantage.

(d) Redistributing, sublicensing, selling, renting, hosting, or providing the Software or a modified version as part of a commercial service, including use by employees, contractors, or agents for such a purpose.

(e) Using the Software to perform paid client work or generate materials intended for commercial distribution, even if the Software is installed or operated through an individual's personal account, personal computer, or privately held credentials.

A free trial, indirect monetization, sponsorship, advertising-supported offering, or provision without a separate line-item software fee does not automatically make an otherwise commercial activity noncommercial. Whether an activity is commercial depends on its objective circumstances.

**The trigger is the purpose and beneficiary of the use, not the identity of the account holder or the method of installation.**

